 "meta": {
  "what": "Price levels of what Türkiye buys from Russia (crude, oil products, pipeline gas, LNG, coal, other fossil, non-fuel goods), 2018-2026, built so that crude and gas do not rest on the partner-hidden Turkish customs lines. Drop-in replacement for prices.json countries.TUR (same fields) plus a gas_prices.json-style pipeline series.",
  "units": "index = level / own 2018-2021 average (= 1); levels EUR/t (crude CIF Turkey, products, coal) or EUR/MWh GCV (gas); paid, at_base_prices, windfall in EUR bn nominal; 2026 = January-August, not annualised; USD at ECB yearly averages 2018 1.181, 2019 1.1195, 2020 1.142, 2021 1.183, 2022 1.053, 2023 1.081, 2024 1.082, 2025 1.13, 2026 1.16.",
  "method": "Crude: EPDK crude imports from Russia (t) x (Russian MinFin Urals + Black Sea freight). Pipeline gas: EPDK volumes from Russia split into long-term and spot pipeline gas; long-term priced 70% TTF / 30% oil formula from 2022 (Gazprom-BOTAS contracts renegotiated in 2021 to include hub indexation: OIES, CGEP), oil formula = 0.418 x 9-month Brent lagged 1 month x Turkish factor 0.85; spot pipeline gas at 95% of TTF; central = mean of this contract model and the gas value implied by Turkish customs (chapter 27 from Russia, partner visible, minus visible headings, minus crude and LNG). Base 2018-2021 from the same two sources plus the reported 2020 TurkStream price. LNG: EPDK Russian spot LNG x CREA price, European Russian-LNG base. Products and coal: partner-visible Turkish customs unit values, kept from prices.json and checked against CREA. Non-fuel goods: kept from prices.json.",
  "review": "Not yet reviewed by a person."
 },
